  "body": "There is currently no way for a user to be synapse admin based on a \"role\" mapping from the OIDC server, which means manually changing roles in the postgres db after said person has logged in. It would be great if it supported \"role\" mapping right out of the box so when user logs in they are granted synapse admin, according to the configuration in the OIDC server (in my case keycloak).\r\n\r\nBackground: we were hoping to rollout to about 700 clients, between 8 different organizations we currently support. They will all have their own federated server. There are about 50-60 admins in total (not including the 2 admins from our company), that would all need admin access to their federated server so they can manage their internal rooms. Right now it looks like I would need to manually edit each user in postgres after they have logged in.",
